From 3604e7b8f9b18f53dd29740df244be844e44167e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:27:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-161a: a progress bar while F5 builds -- from
 CMake's own progress folder, F5 itself unchanged (0.161.0, no version change)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20261002: 「編譯進度可以有個進度條嗎?」. The designer's own green play button had one; F5 did not.
F5's preLaunchTask calls cmake directly (the 08:31 wrapper tools\build_with_status.ps1 on the F5 path made F5 not
start on this machine and was reverted at 09:40, 0192f29) -- so nothing on the F5 path is touched here:
- lib/buildwatch.js: CMake's Makefile generators keep <build>\CMakeFiles\Progress\ during a build (count.txt = the
  target's steps, one file per finished step; make's "[ 45%]" is counted from it); a build that ends removes it, a
  failed / stopped one leaves it. cmakeProgress(dir), runningCMake(root, since). Also reads the wrapper's
  web\JSON\runtime\boot_build.js if it is ever written again.
- extension.js: a build task's start / end (vscode.tasks.onDidStart/EndTaskProcess, not the designer's own); every
  second while one runs, the newest build* folder's progress -> a VS Code notification bar (no Cancel: F5's build is
  VS Code's task); the folder gone = "建置完成" in the status bar; the task ended with it left = "建置沒有完成", said.
  Read only: it never starts, stops or changes a build.
Tests: lib 181/181 (status file; a temporary build folder 9/20 = 45%), extension 223/223 (a simulated F5 build task:
25% -> 75%, done; a second one failing), probe 7/7 + tab tree 7/7, panels all pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
